A column schema.sql no longer makes would lose its values: refused, and
nothing changes.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  name TEXT NOT NULL,
  note TEXT
) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup', 'hot');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  name TEXT NOT NULL
) STRICT;

== error
column `dish.note` is in the database, not in schema.sql: its values would go. Keep it, or drop it on purpose: `-- @drop column dish note` in schema.sql. (A rename is a drop and a new one: the values do not follow.)
